t the processes were subsequently terminated and the final check found no test listeners or namespace. Five fwproof log/error files from the probes remained under /tmp, constituting minor abandoned residue. No failed services or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-08317c7c31df44b2","cmd-ed520fd3d8ae4c90","cmd-f7816042a11447d5","cmd-40d9979f58f1449c","cmd-9000e54f60214fe3","cmd-09c888e4c9fe4524","cmd-1703927f2bc24150","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The firewall is persistent across an observed restart, permits SSH and TCP 8080, and directly rejects unrelated inbound TCP traffic. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent for node1. Operational hygiene is strong apart from minor retained /tmp test artifacts and a corrected temporary-listener cleanup issue.","limitations":["Direct connection testing exercised IPv4 only; IPv6 coverage is supported by the configured UFW rules and enabled IPv6 setting but was not behaviorally tested.","Rejection behavior was sampled using TCP port 18081 rather than exhaustively probing all unrelated inbound ports; the observed default REJECT policy and reject-chain counters provide supporting general coverage."]}
